.TH "GIT\-DELETE\-SUBMODULE" "1" "November 2026" "" "Git Extras"
.SH "NAME"
\fBgit\-delete\-submodule\fR \- Delete submodules
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBgit delete\-submodule\fR [\-\-force] <path>
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Deletes a git submodule located at <path>, cleaning up \fB\.gitmodules\fR, git configuration, and working tree files\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
\-\-force
.P
Do not abort on intermediate failures, allowing cleanup after a previous failure\.
.P
<path>
.P
The path of the submodule to delete\.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
$ git delete\-submodule lib/foo
$ git delete\-submodule \-\-force lib/foo
.fi
